This theorem has a direct consequence for the strong variant. Because any strong sEF$c$ allocation must also satisfy weak sEF$c$, the impossibility of achieving weak sEF$c$ under certain conditions immediately implies that strong sEF$c$ allocations cannot exist under the same conditions. 
