where we used Lemma~\ref{lem:recur1} and \eqref{eq:seedEx} to directly compute $s_\infty$. 
If $s_\infty>C/\la,$ then there is no overshadowing class as it would not obstruct the peaks of $\mu_{\bE_k,\bf{b}}$ for large $k.$ Hence, we must have 
\[ s_\infty  \leq C/\la.\]
We now compare the line $s_\infty$ to the line $s_0.$ In particular, since $\bE_0 = (2;1,1; W(3,1))$ the line $\ell_0$ has equation
\[
