Using homomorphisms of quandles we can prove that the trefoil knot is non-trivial.

\begin{example}\label{trefoil-coloring-r3}
{\rm
Let $K$ be the trefoil knot (see Figure \ref{Trefoil knot}).  Then its knot quandle has a presentation
$$
Q(K) = \big\langle x, y, z   \, \mid \,  x * y = z, ~y * z = x,~ z * x = y \big\rangle.
$$

