Let $(X,r)$ be a solution to the Yang--Baxter equation. Figure \ref{2dboundary} depicts the $2$-dimensional cube ${\mathcal I}_2$. The top two edges form the initial path, and the edges are colored by $x,y \in X$. The bottom edges are colored by $\sigma_x(y)$ and $\tau_y(x)$, so that these assignments indeed defines a Yang--Baxter coloring of the cube ${\mathcal I}_2$. Hence, the boundary homomorphism in this case is given by 
\begin{equation}\label{dim two boundary homo}
\partial_2 (x,y) = (x) + (y) - \sigma_x(y) - \tau_y(x).
