\subsection{T1 Cell}
The T1 (adder) cell is an SFQ circuit with synchronous sum and asynchronous carry output \cite{razmkhahBook, bairamkulovT1}. An SFQ pulse appears on the carry output when two or more input pulses are present, while an SFQ pulse is generated on the sum output when an odd number of input pulses are present. The related circuit with a simulation showing the generation of asynchronous carry output and synchronous sum output is provided in Fig. \ref{fig:bvmT1all}.

