Anomaly Detection in general, tries to answer whether a sample belongs to the class "normal" or not. Thus shape approximation is perfectly suited to anomaly detection. We evaluate this in Figure~\ref{fig:better} using 7 recent neural network (and thus function approximation-based) anomaly detection algorithms on the benchmark datasets proposed by a recent survey paper~\cite{surveyzhao}. We find that Polyra Swarms outperforms all our competitors and does so significantly for most of them.


