We follow the same rationale by eliciting a beta prior with parameters $\alpha$ and $\beta$ and  mean $\alpha/(\alpha + \beta) = (1/2)(n/n_0)$ and coefficient of variation $1$.
This gives $\alpha \approx 0.77$ and $\beta \approx 6.21$.
