As described in Section~\hyperref[sec:LEAP]{2.8}, fitting the latent exchangeability prior (LEAP) involves setting the hyperparameters $K$ and $\bm{\alpha}_0$, which are denoted as \texttt{K} and \texttt{prob.conc} in function \texttt{glm.leap}, respectively. We may sample from the posterior under the LEAP as follows:
\begin{verbatim}
fit.leap <- glm.leap(
  formula = formula, family = family, data.list = the.data,
  K = 2, prob.conc = rep(1, 2),
  iter_warmup = iter_warmup, iter_sampling = iter_sampling,
  chains = nchains, parallel_chains = ncores,
  refresh = 0
)
