Using this formulation, Ying defines a Complete Partial Order (CPO), which orders the operators within the Fock space based on the number of guard copies that these operators act on.
As a result, the semantics of a recursive program demonstrates a monotonically continuous order, which, in turn, allows for the existence of a fixed point.

