  \label{fig:tsne}
\end{figure}

\par Figure \ref{fig:tsne} visualizes t-SNE plots of class pixel features extracted from an MiT-B5 \cite{Xie21} encoder loaded with ImageNet-pretrained weights at the start of training (right) and at the end of training using CoPT (left) implemented on top of MIC \cite{Hoyer23}. Images from Cityscapes val set are fed to the models. CoPT encourages feature embeddings to be more distinct from each other as can be seen by the greater separation between data points. There are fewer outliers in CoPT versus ImageNet e.g. the traffic sign, building and wall classes showing the regularization of the latent space. 

\subsection{Mistral 7B Sentence Embedding}
\label{sec:mistral_emb}

\par When using Mistral 7B \cite{Jiang23a} as CoPT's text embedding method in Section \ref{sec:ablations}, we generate a single text embedding for each prompt by averaging together Mistral's embedding for each word in the prompt. Mistral 7B outputs a single embedding for each word because it was trained for next token prediction and not designed to generate sentence embeddings.

