As shown in Table \ref{tab:A6}, in the CW test, Ridge, PLS, GLM, \(Ensemble_{op}\), and \(Ensemble_{\theta=0.9}\) show no significant difference from OLS, while all other sophisticated models outperform OLS significantly. In the MCS test, only Ridge and RF are comparable to OLS, with all other models performing significantly better. In the GW test, Ridge is the only model not significantly different from OLS, while all other models show superior performance. Ridge is the only model that fails to achieve statistically significant improvement over OLS across all three tests, likely due to its underperformance in strong-factor environments. Overall, these results highlight that, apart from Ridge, our sophisticated machine learning models outperform OLS at least in one of the three tests, demonstrating their robustness and predictive power.


